  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "According to the conflict report, Ukrainian drones struck the Crimean Bridge for the second day in a row, killing two people and prompting Russian authorities to close vehicle traffic again.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-17:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "As Wikipedia records, in the early hours of 17 November the bridge was struck again, collapsing the arch structure supporting the main span as well as the road span itself.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386577387:71"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The Crimean Bridge, also called Kerch Strait Bridge or Kerch Bridge, is a double road and rail bridge spanning the Kerch Strait between Krasnodar Krai and the Kerch Peninsula of Crimea.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386577387:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The reports place the bridge over the Kerch Strait.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-17:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "Russia is also named in the reports.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-17:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:42Z",
      "text": "English Wikipedia recorded 63,755 readers of the article on 17 November 2026, about 452 times the usual daily figure of 141.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Crimean_Bridge:2026-11-17",
        "views:en:Crimean_Bridge:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:49Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 11 languages, and after English the most readers were in Russian, with 39,704.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Crimean_Bridge:2026-11-17",
        "views:ru:Крымский_мост:2026-11-17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:56Z",
      "text": "Each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, and a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:ru:Крымский_мост:2026-11-17",
        "views:de:Krim-Brücke:2026-11-17",
        "views:pl:Most_Krymski:2026-11-17",
        "views:fr:Pont_de_Crimée:2026-11-17",
        "views:ja:クリミア大橋:2026-11-17",
        "views:it:Ponte_di_Crimea:2026-11-17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:06Z",
      "text": "The story is reported by Reuters and Türkiye Today.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-17:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:14Z",
      "text": "France 24 ran the headline “🔴 Live: Kerch Bridge to occupied Crimea closed after Ukrainian strikes collapse road section.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:ed14a50b56b5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:20Z",
      "text": "The Guardian ran the headline “How Ukraine struck the Kerch bridge, a symbol of Putin’s rule.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:guardian:b3d40d0737d8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:26Z",
